name: sim.exportMesh
description: Exports a mesh to a file
luaSynopsis: sim.exportMesh(int fileformat, string pathAndFilename, int options, float scalingFactor, list vertices, list indices)
pythonSynopsis: sim.exportMesh(int fileformat, string pathAndFilename, int options, float scalingFactor, float[] vertices, int[] indices)
inputs:
1. fileformat: the fileformat to export to:
    - 0: OBJ format
    - 3: TEXT STL format
    - 4: BINARY STL format
    - 5: COLLADA format
    - 6: TEXT PLY format
    - 7: BINARY PLY format
2. pathAndFilename: the location of the file to create.
3. options: keep at 0
4. scalingFactor: the scaling factor to apply to the vertices to export
5. vertices: an array of vertice arrays. See the example below
6. indices: an array of indice arrays. See the example below
outputs:
replacedBy:
- simAssimp functions
